WEBVTT

00:54:27.454 --> 00:54:33.121
And so, you know, ultimately you can
picture processes where they do better.

00:54:33.329 --> 00:54:39.413
And I I believe that most engineers, for
example, work in Silicon Valley.

00:54:39.413 --> 00:54:43.954
Companies are actually good people
who want to design great products

00:54:43.954 --> 00:54:47.246
for humanity. I think that the people
who run these companies want to be

00:54:47.246 --> 00:54:49.038
a net contribution to humanity.

00:54:49.038 --> 00:54:51.788
It's we've we've rushed really quickly

00:54:51.788 --> 00:54:53.996
and design stuff without thinking
it through properly.

00:54:53.996 --> 00:54:55.788
And it's led to a mess up.

00:54:55.954 --> 00:54:58.788
So it's like, OK, don't move fast,
break things,

00:54:58.913 --> 00:55:02.371
slow down and build beautiful
things that are built on